{
  "about": "One submission section composed and saved (DEFINE, SUB, JSON, PROJECT, CT, INPUT): what refuses a composition before any specification is read, what its metadata refutes, how it rechecks a published dataset, and where its save publishes each file. Moved from file_resources.rs's shared_define module. A case stages a benchmark's files and takes a published dataset from the benchmark's expected/ files, as the tests copied them; the two refusals that come before any specification is read stage the project file and the published dataset alone, since their tests deleted the specification. Each case compares what its test compared: rows found by their cause are among the issues, and a refused composition's saved is {}, the absent define.xml and transport file its test asserted. A document no authored file holds, such as the Define-XML of an edited or a metadata-only composition, is stated by the parts its test compared, each selected whole (select): an element from its start tag through its end tag, an attribute's value or a JSON value, and the complete list a path selects stands for a test's count or absence. The nine migrated document selections stage only the specification and project files their original tests copied, plus the published dataset where required. Raw input files remain unavailable, retaining the metadata-only tests' proof that composing metadata needs no raw study inputs. The unused-terminology API sidecar also proves that input and acrf.pdf remain absent, including empty directories. The tests that stay in file_resources.rs compare what a composition holds and reads between its preparation and its save, or stay by design. The three compositions that relocate the DM benchmark's dataset publish the benchmark's own documents: nothing either document writes depends on the specification's path, and each names the other relative to itself, the transport file beside the document (JSON-1).",
  "documents": {
    "study_lb": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: spec\nmodel: SDTM\ndomain: LB\nkeys: [USUBJID, LBTESTCD]\ninput: {RAW: raw.csv}\noutput: {path: lb.csv, columns: [USUBJID, LBTESTCD]}\ncolumns:\n  - name: USUBJID\n    type: str\n    label: Unique Subject Identifier\n    derivation: RAW.USUBJID\n    submission: {core: Req, length: 20, origins: [{type: Assigned, source: Sponsor}]}\n  - name: LBTESTCD\n    type: str\n    label: Lab Test or Examination Short Name\n    derivation: RAW.LBTESTCD\n    submission: {core: Req, length: 8, origins: [{type: Assigned, source: Sponsor}]}\nsubmission: {label: Laboratory Test Results, class: FINDINGS, structure: One record per lab test per subject, repeating: true}\n",
    "study_adlb": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: spec\nmodel: ADaM\ndomain: ADLB\nkeys: [USUBJID, PARAMCD]\ninput: {LB: lb.csv}\noutput: {path: adlb.csv, columns: [USUBJID, PARAMCD, SRCDOM]}\ncolumns:\n  - name: USUBJID\n    type: str\n    label: Unique Subject Identifier\n    derivation: LB.USUBJID\n    submission: {core: Req, mandatory: true, length: 20, origins: [{type: Predecessor, description: LB.USUBJID}]}\n  - name: PARAMCD\n    type: str\n    label: Parameter Code\n    derivation: LB.LBTESTCD\n    submission: {core: Req, mandatory: true, length: 8, origins: [{type: Predecessor, description: LB.LBTESTCD}]}\n  - name: SRCDOM\n    type: str\n    label: Source Data\n    derivation: \"'LB'\"\n    submission: {core: Perm, mandatory: false, length: 8, inventory_vocabulary: true, origins: [{type: Assigned}]}\nsubmission: {label: Laboratory Analysis Dataset, class: BASIC DATA STRUCTURE, structure: One record per subject per parameter, repeating: true}\n",
    "cross_section_project": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: project\nstudy: {id: STUDY, name: Study, description: Cross-section witness, protocol_name: Protocol}\nadam:\n  standards: [{name: ADaMIG, version: '1.3', status: Final}]\n  specs: [adlb.yaml]\n  define: define.xml\n  transport: dataset_json\n  source_system_version: '1.0'\nsdtm:\n  standards: [{name: SDTMIG, version: '3.4', status: Final}]\n  specs: [sdtm/lb.yaml]\n  define: sdtm/define.xml\n"
  },
